   "body": "State on `dev-swift` (steward ext/opus-helper1, 2026-10-29). **Partly done; the issue stays open.**\n\nDone:\n- **Engine:** LOT-167 (#291, merged as `0f94f4e`) added `PageNavigation.isExact`. It is set by `TopicListPager`: exact for a short pager or no pager, a lower bound for any window. Records stored before the flag decode as a lower bound. The spec is `docs/features/FEAT-003.md`, and #104 is closed.\n- **App:** the lists show \"Page N\" and never a total (`thePagerNeverClaimsATotal`, LOT-082).\n\nLeft (app side, per `docs/features/FEAT-003.md` \"Screens and states\"):\n1. Show \"N / total\" in the list header only when `navigation.isExact`.\n2. \"Dernière page\" (swipe, menu): enabled only when `isExact`, otherwise disabled. This depends on the list actions and the page navigator: LOT-125 (#216) and LOT-110 (#201), both blocked today.\n3. The topic row's page count (`sujetCase4`) stays exact and usable for a topic's last page. Check this when the row UI exists.\n\nItem 1 is small: App code only, CI builds the App, no capture needed. It can be delegated to an external contributor (Bybifok), with an Opus review if the author is Sonnet, Fable if Opus. Items 2–3 follow LOT-110 and LOT-125.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
